  "text": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "Ann is Tom's cousin. She comes to the house in the morning. She has a big bag. Tom opens the door. \"Hello, Ann!\" says Dad. \"Hi, Ann!\" says Lily. \"Good morning, Ann,\" says Mom. Ann smiles. \"Hello, family!\" she says. Pip says, \"Woof!\"",
      "Lily has a small board. She has a pen and an eraser. \"Ann, how do you say hello?\" asks Lily. \"I can say hi,\" says Ann. \"I can say hello too.\" Lily writes an example on the board. \"Hi, hello, good morning!\" \"Hi and hello are friends!\" says Tom. Lily cleans the board with the eraser. \"Now you write one,\" she says.",
      "Then Ann goes home. \"Bye, Tom!\" says Ann. \"Goodbye, Ann!\" says Lily. \"See you, Ann!\" says Dad. \"Thank you, Ann!\" says Tom. \"Please come again!\" says Mom. Ann waves her hand. Ann is happy. Tom is happy too. \"Woof, woof!\" says Pip. Do you say hello to your family?"
    ],
    "summary": "Tom's cousin Ann visits in the morning, and the family says hello in different ways. Lily writes the greetings on a board, and Ann says goodbye at the end.",
